.\"
.TH LINUXCNCLCD "9" "2026-07-31" "LinuxCNC Documentation" "HAL Component"

.SH NAME
linuxcnclcd \- operator interface on an LCDproc character display

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBload linuxcnclcd [server=\fIHOST\fB] [port=\fIN\fB] [delay=\fISECONDS\fB] [autostart=1] [nc_files=\fIDIR\fB] [milltask_instance=\fINAME\fB]\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBlinuxcnclcd\fR drives a small operator panel on a character display and
keypad \(em originally the Matrix Orbital MX4 series, but any display an
LCDproc server (\fBLCDd\fR) supports will do, over serial, USB or anything
else LCDd handles.  The layout assumes 4 lines of 20 characters.
.P
The module talks to LCDd over TCP; it does not touch the display hardware
itself, so LCDd must be running and configured for the display.  It exports
no HAL pins.  Machine status comes from the \fBemcstat\fR GMI API and
commands go out through \fBemccmd\fR, both provided by \fBmilltask\fR \(em so
milltask must be loaded first.
.P
If LCDd is not reachable when the module starts, or the display goes away
later, the module retries the connection every two seconds and rebuilds its
screens when it gets back in.

.SH PARAMETERS
.TP
\fBserver=\fIHOST\fR
Host running LCDd.  Default \fBlocalhost\fR.
.TP
\fBport=\fIN\fR
LCDd port.  Default \fB13666\fR.
.TP
\fBdelay=\fISECONDS\fR
Pause before each protocol send, to keep from overrunning a slow display.
Default \fB0.005\fR.
.TP
\fBautostart=1\fR
Reset ESTOP and switch the machine on when the display first connects.
This happens once per module start \(em a later reconnect does not repeat
it, so a display dropping out cannot clear an ESTOP set in the meantime.
Off by default.
.TP
\fBnc_files=\fIDIR\fR
Directory whose \fB.ngc\fR files fill the File/Open menu.  Defaults to
\fB[DISPLAY]PROGRAM_PREFIX\fR, and to the configured nc_files directory when
that is not set.  A file whose name contains whitespace or brace characters
is left out of the menu, because the name would not survive the LCDproc
protocol intact.
.TP
\fBmilltask_instance=\fINAME\fR
Instance name to look the \fBemcstat\fR and \fBemccmd\fR APIs up under.
Default \fBmilltask\fR.

.SH MENU
.TP
\fBFile\fR \(-> \fBOpen\fR
Lists the \fB.ngc\fR files in the program directory; selecting one switches to
auto mode and opens it.
.TP
\fBFile\fR \(-> \fBReload\fR
Reopens the program the controller currently reports as open, whichever
interface opened it.
.TP
\fBView\fR \(-> \fBUnits\fR
What the position display converts to: mm, cm or inch.
.TP
\fBView\fR \(-> \fBCoord\fR
\fBabs\fR shows machine position, \fBrel\fR shows it with the tool length,
G5x, G5x rotation and G92 offsets applied \(em the same order the AXIS DRO
uses.
.TP
\fBRun\fR \(-> \fBFeed Override\fR
Feed override percentage; tracks the controller when changed elsewhere.
.TP
\fBJog\fR \(-> \fBSpeed\fR, \fBMode\fR
Jog velocity in units per minute, and the increment: continuous, 1.0, 0.1,
0.01 or 0.001 in the selected display units.
.TP
\fBSetup\fR \(-> \fBMain Display\fR
Chooses between the position screen and the summary screen (program name,
feed override, spindle speed, current line).
.TP
\fBUtilities\fR \(-> \fBHome\fR
Homes all joints, or X, Y or Z individually.  These are actions rather than a
selection ring, so nothing homes until an entry is chosen.
.TP
\fBUtilities\fR \(-> \fBLimits\fR
\fBOff\fR overrides soft limit checking so a joint can be jogged off a
tripped switch; \fBOn\fR resumes it.  The setting follows the controller,
which clears the override on any mode change out of manual.

.SH KEYS
.TP
\fBLeft\fR / \fBRight\fR
Jog the first joint, continuously or by the selected increment.
.TP
\fBUp\fR / \fBDown\fR
Jog the second joint.
.TP
\fBRun\fR
Run the open program from the start.
.TP
\fBPause\fR
Pause a running program, resume a paused one.
.TP
\fBStop\fR
Abort.
.TP
\fBStep\fR
Run a single line.
.TP
\fBTest\fR
Toggle between manual and auto mode.
.TP
\fBNext\fR / \fBPrev\fR
Step through the jog increments (continuous, 1.0, 0.1, 0.01, 0.001) while in
manual mode on the position screen.
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Home the first three joints, on the position screen.
.TP
\fBEStop\fR
Toggle ESTOP.
.TP
\fBPower\fR
Toggle machine power.

.SH DISPLAY UNITS
Positions are reported by the controller in millimetres regardless of
\fB[TRAJ]LINEAR_UNITS\fR, and the View/Units menu selects what the display
converts them to.

.SH SEE ALSO
\fBLCDd\fR(8), \fBmilltask\fR(9)

Much more information about LinuxCNC and HAL is available in the LinuxCNC
and HAL User Manuals.

